<div class="context-box">
<strong>Context:</strong> Arhan is convinced by Célia's CRM but finds the price too high. In each scenario, Célia uses a different approach to handle the price objection and close the sale.
  <br/><strong>Instructions:</strong> Complete the grid by analysing each scenario. The hints guide you — it is up to you to formulate the analysis.
</div>
<div style="overflow-x:auto;">
<table class="g-table">
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Criterion</th>
<th class="h1">Scenario 1</th>
<th class="h1">Scenario 2</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<!-- 1. Approche globale -->
<tr>
<td>1. Célia's overall approach</td>
<td>
<div class="hint-label">Hint</div>
<div class="hint-box">Count how many discounts Célia grants in a row. Who is leading the negotiation — Célia or Arhan?</div>
</td>
<td>
<div class="hint-label">Hint</div>
<div class="hint-box">Before talking about price, what does Célia talk about first? What figure does she use?</div>
</td>
</tr>
<!-- 2. Traitement objection prix -->
<tr>
<td>2. How Célia handles the price objection</td>
<td>
<div class="hint-label">Hint</div>
<div class="hint-box">How long does Célia hold out before offering a discount? What happens when Arhan asks for more?</div>
</td>
<td>
<div class="hint-label">Hint</div>
<div class="hint-box">Célia mentions a "+10% customer retention" — why does this argument change Arhan's perception of the price?</div>
</td>
</tr>
<!-- 3. Contreparties -->
<tr>
<td>3. What Célia gets in return</td>
<td>
<div class="hint-label">Hint</div>
<div class="hint-box">Who suggests the customer testimonial — Célia or Arhan? What does that say about Célia's stance?</div>
</td>
<td>
<div class="hint-label">Hint</div>
<div class="hint-box">Logo + testimonial + 3-year commitment: what is the marketing value of these concessions in return for Célia's company?</div>
</td>
</tr>
<!-- 4. Durée d'engagement -->
<tr>
<td>4. Length of the commitment obtained</td>
<td>
<div class="hint-label">Hint</div>
<div class="hint-box">What is the length of the signed contract? Compare with scenario 2.</div>
</td>
<td>
<div class="hint-label">Hint</div>
<div class="hint-box">3-year commitment — how did Célia make this length acceptable to Arhan?</div>
</td>
</tr>
<!-- 5. Posture commerciale -->
<tr>
<td>5. Célia's sales stance</td>
<td>
<div class="hint-label">Hint</div>
<div class="hint-box">Accommodating or proactive?</div>
</td>
<td>
<div class="hint-label">Hint</div>
<div class="hint-box">Accommodating or proactive?</div>
</td>
</tr>
<!-- VERDICT -->
<tr class="verdict-row">
<td>Verdict</td>
<td></td>
<td></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<!-- Questions BTS -->
<div class="q-section">
<h2>Discussion Questions — Group Analysis (BTS / BUT)</h2>
<div class="q-grid">
<div class="q-item">
<strong>Q1.</strong> In scenario 1, Célia makes 3 successive concessions (volume discount, preferential rate, 5% discount). If you were Arhan, what more would you have asked for — and why would you have been right to do so?
      <div class="q-hint">Hint: when a seller gives way 3 times in a row, what perception does that create in the buyer?</div>
</div>
<div class="q-item">
<strong>Q2.</strong> In scenario 2, Arhan refuses a 2-year commitment. Célia does not look for an alternative and moves on to another proposal. What intermediate length could she have proposed, and in exchange for what?
      <div class="q-hint">Hint: between 1 and 2 years, is there possible middle ground?</div>
</div>
<div class="q-item">
<strong>Q3.</strong> What is the precise moment in scenario 2 when Arhan stops seeing the price as a problem and starts seeing it as an investment? Quote Célia's exact sentence.
      <div class="q-hint">Hint: look for the passage where Célia mentions "+10% customer retention" and its impact on revenue.</div>
</div>
<div class="q-item">
<strong>Q4.</strong> If Célia had to negotiate a 4th time with Arhan, combining the best practices of the 2 scenarios, what would her first 3 actions be, in order?
      <div class="q-hint">Hint: think about the sequence ROI → concession → commitment. Which scenario does what first?</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div><!-- fin tab-bts -->
