<!-- Questions Mastère -->
<div class="q-section">
<h2>Discussion Questions — Group Analysis (Master's)</h2>
<div class="q-grid">
<div class="q-item">
<strong>Q1.</strong> Analysing the 2 scenarios through the lens of principled negotiation (Fisher &amp; Ury), which one best applies the principle "separate the people from the problem"? Justify with extracts from the dialogue.
      <div class="q-hint">Hint: in which scenario does Célia rephrase Arhan's interests before defending her own?</div>
</div>
<div class="q-item">
<strong>Q2.</strong> Calculate the revenue secured by Célia in each scenario over the full length of the commitment, taking the discounts granted into account. Which scenario generates the most net value for Célia's company?
      <div class="q-hint">Hint: base price × (1 − discount %) × length of commitment × number of licences.</div>
</div>
<div class="q-item">
<strong>Q3.</strong> In scenario 2, Arhan refuses the 2-year commitment, citing "flexibility". Propose a SPIN counter-argument (Situation → Problem → Implication → Need-Payoff) that Célia could have used to overcome this objection.
      <div class="q-hint">Hint: what is the cost of flexibility for Arhan? (changing CRM, migration, training...)</div>
</div>
<div class="q-item">
<strong>Q4.</strong> If Arhan shared the 2 scenarios with his CEO, which one would the CEO approve most easily — and why? Analyse from the buyer's point of view, not the seller's.
      <div class="q-hint">Hint: a CEO looks for the best value-for-investment ratio AND commitment security. Which scenario ticks both boxes?</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div><!-- fin tab-mastere -->
<p class="footer">Avatar Sales Academy — CRM negotiation analysis grids · Célia × Arhan · BTS BUT &amp; Master's</p>
</div>
<script>
function switchTab(tab) {
  document.querySelectorAll('.tab-btn').forEach(b => b.classList.remove('active'));
  document.querySelectorAll('.tab-content').forEach(c => c.classList.remove('active'));
  document.getElementById('tab-' + tab).classList.add('active');
  document.querySelector('.tab-btn[onclick*="' + tab + '"]').classList.add('active');
}
</script>
</body>
